CloudBurrow patch 41 to github.com/goccy/bigquery-emulator v0.8.1
(cloudburrow/cloudburrow#1487). Applies after patch 0037; needs
googlesqlite patch 0051.

Since patch 0034 the engine's clock follows CloudBurrow's front's, which
compat tests move forward, but the emulator still stamped the times it
reports by the system clock: a dataset's and a table's creationTime and
lastModifiedTime, a job's startTime and endTime, and a Storage API read
session's expireTime and a write stream's createTime and commitTime. So a
table made after the clock was advanced was older than the
CURRENT_TIMESTAMP() of its creation, and a test comparing the two failed.
The patch stamps each by googlesqlite.Now, the engine's clock.
server/front_clock_times_test.go fails without the patch and passes with
it.

